because genes and environments are inextricably intertwined. You're a fraternal twin yourself. How has that experience as a twin influenced your research? Well, being a fraternal twin, I was always fascinated with being a twin, And although I never got the adulation that identical twins get when people meet them. But I knew from a very early age that there had to be something fundamentally different about us because we shared so many experiences in common and yet we were so different in appearance and our interest,

